  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "If $H=[\\begin{aligned}5 & c \\\\ c & 5\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $c.$",
  "worked_solution": "The matrix $H$ is singular if and only if $det(H)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(H) & =5\\cdot 5-c\\cdot c \\\\  & =25-{c}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25-{c}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =25 \\\\ c & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $c$ are $c=\\pm 5.$",
